===== Hardware =====
==== Buttons ====
-> [[docs:guide-user:hardware:hardware.button]] on howto use and configure the hardware button(s).
Here, we merely name the buttons, so we can use them in the above Howto.

The EnGenius ENS202EXT has a single button:

^ BUTTON   ^ Event   ^
| Reset    | reset   |

==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty!

To open the case:
  - Remove the antennas.
  - Remove the bottom cover.
  - Unscrew the phillips screw what got visible after removing the bottom cover.
  - Unscrew the 2 nuts of the antenna connectors
  - Push a little bit the antenna connectors into the housing and back. This will free 2 rubber gaskets at the antenna connectors.
  - Remove the gaskets and then push the antenna connectors inside again. This will nicely remove the whole PCB out of the housing.


//PCB pictures://\\
{{:media:engenius:ens202ext_pcb_front.jpg?0x500|}}
{{:media:engenius:ens202ext_pcb_back.jpg?0x500|}}


==== Serial ====
-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.

Solder a header or direct wires to the contacts marked as TX,RX and GND on the picture below.\\
Use a serial adapter with TTL 3.3V signal levels. Not a standard RS-232 port. This will damage the serial port of the device due the high voltage levels.\\
Connect the **TX pin** of the serial adapter with the **RX pin** of the PCB, and the **RX pin** of the serial adapter with the **TX pin** of the PCB.\\

Bits per second: **115200**\\
Data bits: **8**\\
Parity: **None**\\
Stop bits: **1**\\
Flow control: **None**\\

{{:media:engenius:ens202ext_serial_pcb.jpg?400|}}


